[
  {
    "endpoint": "/v1/users/{id}",
    "method": "GET",
    "output_encoding": "json",
    "backend": [
      {
        "url_pattern": "/users/{id}",
        "encoding": "json",
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@comment": "A customer's orders, each with its own participants, in three calls however many orders there are: 0 the orders; 1 the events of all of them; 2 every participant in one batch. The generic Lua in lua/collections.lua does the looping config cannot: pluck collects ids for the next call, attach gives each order the users from its own events. The key names below say what joins to what.",
    "endpoint": "/v1/customers/{id}/orders",
    "method": "GET",
    "output_encoding": "json",
    "extra_config": {
      "proxy": {
        "sequential": true
      },
      "modifier/lua-proxy": {
        "sources": [
          "/etc/krakend/collections.lua"
        ],
        "post": "local r = response.load() attach(r, { parents = 'orders', key = 'id', children = 'events', child_key = 'order_id', ids = 'participant_ids', lookup = 'customers', lookup_key = 'customer_id', into = 'participants' }) drop(r, { 'order_ids', 'events', 'participant_ids', 'customers', 'requested', 'returned', 'missing' })",
        "allow_open_libs": false
      }
    },
    "backend": [
      {
        "url_pattern": "/customers/{id}/orders",
        "encoding": "json",
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ],
        "extra_config": {
          "modifier/lua-backend": {
            "sources": [
              "/etc/krakend/collections.lua"
            ],
            "post": "pluck(response.load(), 'orders', 'id', 'order_ids')",
            "allow_open_libs": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "url_pattern": "/events?order_id={resp0_order_ids}",
        "encoding": "json",
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ],
        "extra_config": {
          "modifier/lua-backend": {
            "sources": [
              "/etc/krakend/collections.lua"
            ],
            "post": "pluck(response.load(), 'events', 'participant_ids', 'participant_ids')",
            "allow_open_libs": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "url_pattern": "/users?ids={resp1_participant_ids}",
        "encoding": "json",
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "endpoint": "/v1/customers/{id}",
    "method": "GET",
    "output_encoding": "json",
    "backend": [
      {
        "url_pattern": "/users/{id}",
        "encoding": "json",
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ]
      },
      {
        "url_pattern": "/customers/{id}/orders",
        "encoding": "json",
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "extra_config": {
      "auth/validator": {
        "@comment": "Accepts the token from the Authorization header or, for browser navigation, from the cookie the login page sets.",
        "alg": "RS256",
        "jwk_url": "http://keycloak-keycloakx-http.iam.svc.cluster.local/realms/poc/protocol/openid-connect/certs",
        "issuer": "http://keycloak.localhost:8080/realms/poc",
        "audience": [
          "krakend"
        ],
        "cookie_key": "access_token",
        "cache": true,
        "cache_duration": 900,
        "disable_jwk_security": true
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "@comment": "Users with at least one order. Deciding who counts as a customer is a join of users and orders \u2014 a database question \u2014 so demo-api answers it in one query and the gateway just passes it through.",
    "endpoint": "/v1/customers",
    "method": "GET",
    "output_encoding": "json",
    "backend": [
      {
        "url_pattern": "/customers",
        "encoding": "json",
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@comment": "The other merge style: each backend declares a `group`, so its response stays nested under that name instead of being flattened alongside the other. Compare with /v1/customers/{id}.",
    "endpoint": "/v1/profile/{id}",
    "method": "GET",
    "output_encoding": "json",
    "extra_config": {
      "qos/ratelimit/router": {
        "max_rate": 20,
        "capacity": 20
      }
    },
    "backend": [
      {
        "url_pattern": "/users/{id}",
        "encoding": "json",
        "group": "identity",
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ]
      },
      {
        "url_pattern": "/customers/{id}/orders",
        "encoding": "json",
        "group": "purchases",
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
]
